Subject: Practiced Offense: give the AI a target for the double strike / lifelink part
Why: The AI checks a spell's sub-abilities before casting it. The second half (Pump with
  KWChoice$ Double Strike,Lifelink) reads to PumpAi as +0/+0 with no keyword, because nothing in
  forge-ai looks at KWChoice, so getPumpCreatures finds no creature that would benefit and the
  whole spell is refused (Azorius Momo, baseline: seen in 184 games, cast in 0).
  AILogic$ ContinuousBonus makes PumpAi pick the AI's own creature with the highest power, the
  right target for double strike. The counters half (target yourself) already passed.
Measured: PENDING (filled in from the before/after gauntlets).

